      "note": "Hand-set from general knowledge of the species: a dense, nearly stemless rosette of a hundred or more narrow blue-green leaves 50 cm to 1 m long, spoon-shaped at the base and armed with curved prickles along both edges; old leaves hang as a skirt; a narrow flowering spike 2 to 5 m tall rises most years once the plant is mature. Not fitted to measurements."
